    {
      "id": "1a7b20828dcc7de886228fdcb527df64ab737679",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 666840721,
          "type": null,
          "body": "OK, I'm in the middle of rethinking some of the data types used, given that:\n\n1. Microsoft didn't introduce an `ssize_t` type so that `_read()` and `_write()` could take a `size_t` buffer size argument and return an `ssize_t` result - the return values are `int`, so the biggest size in a `ws_read()` call is 32767 bytes;\n1. `gsize` (not one of the Glib developers' brightest ideas!) is not guaranteed to be equal to `size_t` (it's 32 bits with MSVC, even when building 64-bit, which is bogus).",
          "author": {
            "id": 5636682,
            "username": "guyharris",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Guy Harris",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/1b7c243a9b1d6587a9a9067e5d83aba1e87212df7c4eeae3690f791ecbe4675a?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/guyharris"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-09-02T00:13:29.063Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-09-02T00:13:29.063Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 115003233,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
